---
// BenchmarkResults.astro — Measured, not asserted: judgment benchmarks and cost metrics
// Anchor: benchmarks | Responsive section | No props
---

<section class="benchmark-section">
  <p class="section-moral"><em>Measured, not asserted.</em></p>

  <h2 id="benchmarks">Benchmarks: measured cost and capability</h2>

  <div class="benchmark-grid">
    <!-- Benchmark 1: Judgment accuracy -->
    <div class="benchmark-card">
      <h3>Judgment Accuracy</h3>
      <p class="benchmark-subtitle">39-task judgment benchmark</p>
      <div class="metric-pair">
        <div class="metric">
          <span class="metric-label">Haiku</span>
          <span class="metric-value">39/39</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <span class="metric-label">Opus</span>
          <span class="metric-value">38/39</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="benchmark-note">
        <em>Curated set (N=39) · Haiku at ~1/3 the cost of Opus · Ground truth established by human review</em>
      </p>
      <p class="benchmark-provenance">
        <em><a href="https://github.com/matt82198/aesop/tree/main/bench/results" class="benchmark-link">Real benchmark runs (2026-07-17 + 2026-07-26 ceiling addendum, pinned models; see bench/results/)</a></em>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Benchmark 2: Context enrichment fix rate -->
    <div class="benchmark-card">
      <h3>Context Enrichment</h3>
      <p class="benchmark-subtitle">One-shot fix rate, 360-run A/B</p>
      <div class="metric-single">
        <span class="metric-value">+17pp</span>
        <span class="metric-label">improvement</span>
      </div>
      <p class="benchmark-note">
        <em>43% → 60% · Baseline cost-neutral · Dispatch failure analysis with test output fed back to repair prompts</em>
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p class="benchmark-methodology">
    <em>Methodology:</em> These measurements come from closed experiments within the Aesop project itself. The judgment benchmark is a held-out set graded by human reviewers; the cost A/B was an in-flight dispatch architecture comparison; the frontier slice is a planned measurement against live models. Each publishes its method and its caveats — no post-hoc claim without the data to support it.
  </p>
</section>

<style>
  .benchmark-section {
    margin: var(--space-16) 0;
  }

  .benchmark-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .section-moral {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-normal);
  }

  .section-moral em {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .benchmark-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .benchmark-card {
    padding: var(--space-8);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-secondary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    transition: background-color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out),
                border-color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .benchmark-card {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  .benchmark-card:hover {
    background: var(--color-bg);
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }

  .benchmark-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .benchmark-subtitle {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
  }

  .metric-pair {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .metric {
    flex: 1;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .metric-single {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .metric-label {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
    display: block;
  }

  .metric-value {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    display: block;
  }

  .benchmark-note {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .benchmark-methodology {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-6);
    background-color: var(--color-bg-tertiary);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .benchmark-methodology em {
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .benchmark-provenance {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0 0;
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .benchmark-link {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent);
    transition: color var(--duration-base) var(--ease-out);
  }

  .benchmark-link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-light);
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent-light);
  }

  .benchmark-link:focus {
    outline: var(--focus-ring);
    outline-offset: var(--focus-ring-offset);
  }
</style>
